@*
    Hidden fields the comment spam filter reads (see Blog.Core.Services.CommentSpamFilter).

    - commentToken: the form's signed render time. Proves the form was fetched and tells the filter
      how long the reader spent writing. Issued by CommentFormTokenService in BlogController.Post.
    - contact_ref: a honeypot. Off-screen, unlabeled, excluded from the tab order and from autofill;
      a real reader never sees it, so anything posted in it is a form-filling script.

    Layout-independent by design: inline styles only, no CSS class any of the 20 layouts must define.
*@
@{
    var commentFormToken = ViewData["CommentFormToken"] as string ?? "";
}
<input type="hidden" name="@Blog.Web.Services.CommentFormTokenService.FieldName" value="@commentFormToken" />
<div aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;left:-10000px;top:auto;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;">
    <label for="@Blog.Web.Services.CommentFormTokenService.HoneypotFieldName">Leave this field empty</label>
    <input type="text" id="@Blog.Web.Services.CommentFormTokenService.HoneypotFieldName" name="@Blog.Web.Services.CommentFormTokenService.HoneypotFieldName" value="" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
</div>
